  "details": "my ISP forced my router in IPv6 only, their IPv4 rooting over IPv6 is abismal, i don't have any control over that.\n\nrealtime networking seems to work okish\n\nAPI take ages to respond if at all\n\nthe furthest i got is my already cashed home world after waiting 5 minutes in the login screen, nothing else loads anymore.\n\nmost of the time it just says \"you are in offline testing mode\"\n\nsteps to reproduce:\n\n-dissable IPv4 on your machine\n\nalternatively\n\n-be forced by your ISP on an IPv6 only connection\n\n-try to launch VRC\n\ni suspect more ISPs are going to try to force their custommers on IPv6 only in the near futur especially on celullar connections (i'm using a 4G router)\n\ni think it's important to see this fixed before it become a significant issue for VRC like it is already for me here\n\nEdit: after more investigation it seems to be something else but none of it make sens and's all way over my head, in short: VRC don't work over Buoygues telecom's 4G routers.\n\nEdit 2: if i can reach the home world i have to preload worlds before joining it, otherwise i am stuck in the loading screen at 0b download indefinitely",
